Claude Desktop on Linux

The desktop app on Linux gives you the same Chat, Cowork, and Claude
Code experience as macOS and Windows: parallel sessions, visual diff
review, an integrated terminal and editor, and live app preview.

NOTE: On Slackware this package has been tested to work only in a
Plasma Wayland graphical session started with startkwayland. It is
not known to work in an X11 session started with startx or
startplasma-x11. In those sessions the app may fail to reach the
KDE Wallet keyring, so the sign-in is not saved. If you see this,
try launching it with:
  claude-desktop --password-store=gnome-libsecret
